      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALEX KEEPING (5) was out of the frame on debut then was strongly fancied last time and ran up to betting with a maiden win at this track over 318m (18.41). Safe beginner but tricky box to overcome. Showing good promise and looks a key player again. ANYONE BUT YOU (1) has missed the placings at his last couple but was in the money three back when third (18.62) at Richmond in a Grade 5. Speedy runner and should be in the action early from the inside. Can hit the frame this time. KARINYA SHALL BE (7) won again in another strong performance after leading them home to make it two on end at this track over 318m (18.49). Has good speed and will be prominent from out wide. In great recent form and expected to measure up again. COBRA BEACH (3) can sneak into the finish.",
